## What actually breaks

`tsc` is happy because both defects are type-legal — they're *runtime/engine* contract violations.

| # | Line | Why preview dies |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `await arn` inside `getBucketUrl` | An `Output<T>` is *thenable-ish* only by accident; awaiting it during preview resolves to `undefined` (unknown value) or hangs. The function returns a bare `Promise<string>`, so `bucketEndpoint` is exported as a Promise with no resource dependency edge — Pulumi loses the DAG link and serializes garbage. |
| 2 | `pulumi.output("plain-text-password")` | Wrapping a literal produces `Output<string>` with **`isSecret = false`**. The value is written to state and `pulumi stack output`/the checkpoint in *plaintext*. Also violates AC-3. |

Rule of thumb: **never `await` an `Output`** — use `.apply()` / `pulumi.interpolate` / `pulumi.all([...]).apply(...)`. Only `await` real `Promise`s from provider `get*` invokes (`aws.getCallerIdentity()` etc.), and even then prefer `.then` chained into an Output.

### The two minimal fixes

```ts
// Defect 1 — string interpolation over an Output, dependency-preserving
const bucketUrl = pulumi.interpolate`https://s3.${region}.amazonaws.com/${bucket.bucket}`;

// Defect 2 — secret sourced from encrypted stack config
const dbPassword = config.requireSecret("dbPassword");
```

Set it with `pulumi config set --secret dbPassword '...'` — the ciphertext lands in `Pulumi.<stack>.yaml`, never plaintext in Git.

---

## `index.ts` (full, spec-compliant)

```ts
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
const stack = pulumi.getStack();              // "dev" | "prod"
const isProd = stack === "prod";

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Environment sizing — driven by stack config, not by ambient strings.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const envSpec = {
    dev:  { nodeCount: 2, nodeType: "t3.medium", dbClass: "db.t3.micro",  multiAz: false, replicate: false },
    prod: { nodeCount: 4, nodeType: "t3.large",  dbClass: "db.t3.medium", multiAz: true,  replicate: true  },
}[isProd ? "prod" : "dev"];

const region = config.require("region");
const tags = { Environment: stack, Project: "myapp", ManagedBy: "pulumi" };

// Secret — encrypted at rest in Pulumi.<stack>.yaml (AC-3).
const dbPassword = config.requireSecret("dbPassword");

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// S3 — versioned, SSE, public access fully blocked (AC-1)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const bucket = new aws.s3.BucketV2("app-bucket", {
    bucket: `myapp-assets-${stack}`,
    tags,
});

new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("app-bucket-versioning", {
    bucket: bucket.id,
    versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
});

new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("app-bucket-sse", {
    bucket: bucket.id,
    rules: [{
        applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" },
        bucketKeyEnabled: true,
    }],
});

new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("app-bucket-pab", {
    bucket: bucket.id,
    blockPublicAcls: true,
    blockPublicPolicy: true,
    ignorePublicAcls: true,
    restrictPublicBuckets: true,
});

// Prod only: cross-region replication to us-west-2.
if (envSpec.replicate) {
    const westProvider = new aws.Provider("aws-west", { region: "us-west-2" });

    const replicaBucket = new aws.s3.BucketV2("app-bucket-replica",
        { bucket: `myapp-assets-${stack}-replica`, tags },
        { provider: westProvider });

    new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("app-bucket-replica-versioning", {
        bucket: replicaBucket.id,
        versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
    }, { provider: westProvider });

    const replRole = new aws.iam.Role("s3-replication-role", {
        assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [{ Effect: "Allow", Principal: { Service: "s3.amazonaws.com" }, Action: "sts:AssumeRole" }],
        }),
        tags,
    });

    // Scoped ARNs — no wildcard actions, no wildcard resources (AC-4).
    new aws.iam.RolePolicy("s3-replication-policy", {
        role: replRole.id,
        policy: pulumi.all([bucket.arn, replicaBucket.arn]).apply(([src, dst]) => JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [
                { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:GetReplicationConfiguration", "s3:ListBucket"], Resource: src },
                { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication", "s3:GetObjectVersionAcl", "s3:GetObjectVersionTagging"], Resource: `${src}/*` },
                { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:ReplicateObject", "s3:ReplicateDelete", "s3:ReplicateTags"], Resource: `${dst}/*` },
            ],
        })),
    });

    new aws.s3.BucketReplicationConfig("app-bucket-replication", {
        role: replRole.arn,
        bucket: bucket.id,
        rules: [{
            id: "replicate-all",
            status: "Enabled",
            filter: {},
            deleteMarkerReplication: { status: "Enabled" },
            destination: { bucket: replicaBucket.arn, storageClass: "STANDARD" },
        }],
    });
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Networking
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const vpc = new aws.ec2.DefaultVpc("default-vpc", { tags });
const subnetIds = aws.ec2.getSubnetsOutput({
    filters: [{ name: "vpc-id", values: [vpc.id] }],
}).ids;   // Output, not an awaited Promise.

const dbSg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("db-sg", {
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    description: "Postgres from VPC only",
    ingress: [{ protocol: "tcp", fromPort: 5432, toPort: 5432, cidrBlocks: [vpc.cidrBlock] }],
    egress: [{ protocol: "-1", fromPort: 0, toPort: 0, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
    tags,
});

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// RDS (AC-2)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const dbSubnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup("db-subnets", { subnetIds, tags });

const db = new aws.rds.Instance("app-db", {
    identifier: `myapp-${stack}`,
    engine: "postgres",
    engineVersion: "16.1",
    instanceClass: envSpec.dbClass,
    allocatedStorage: 20,
    dbName: "appdb",
    username: "appuser",
    password: dbPassword,
    dbSubnetGroupName: dbSubnets.name,
    vpcSecurityGroupIds: [dbSg.id],
    multiAz: envSpec.multiAz,
    storageEncrypted: true,
    publiclyAccessible: false,
    deletionProtection: true,
    backupRetentionPeriod: isProd ? 30 : 7,
    skipFinalSnapshot: false,
    finalSnapshotIdentifier: `myapp-${stack}-final`,
    applyImmediately: !isProd,
    tags,
});

// Connection string stays a secret Output — secret-ness propagates through apply.
const dbConnectionString = pulumi.interpolate`postgresql://appuser:${dbPassword}@${db.endpoint}/appdb`;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EKS (AC-5)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const cluster = new eks.Cluster("app-cluster", {
    name: `myapp-${stack}`,
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    subnetIds,
    nodeGroupOptions: {
        instanceType: envSpec.nodeType,
        desiredCapacity: envSpec.nodeCount,
        minSize: envSpec.nodeCount,
        maxSize: envSpec.nodeCount * 2,
    },
    createOidcProvider: true,
    tags,
});

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// IAM service identity (AC-4)
//  dev  -> IAM user with programmatic access
//  prod -> IRSA role, OIDC trust, no long-lived keys
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const readAssets = pulumi.all([bucket.arn]).apply(([arn]) => JSON.stringify({
    Version: "2012-10-17",
    Statement: [
        { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"], Resource: `${arn}/*` },
        { Effect: "Allow", Action: ["s3:ListBucket"], Resource: arn },
    ],
}));

let serviceIdentityArn: pulumi.Output<string>;

if (isProd) {
    const oidcArn = cluster.core.oidcProvider!.arn;
    const oidcUrl = cluster.core.oidcProvider!.url;

    const svcRole = new aws.iam.Role("app-service-role", {
        assumeRolePolicy: pulumi.all([oidcArn, oidcUrl]).apply(([arn, url]) => JSON.stringify({
            Version: "2012-10-17",
            Statement: [{
                Effect: "Allow",
                Principal: { Federated: arn },
                Action: "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
                Condition: {
                    StringEquals: {
                        [`${url}:aud`]: "sts.amazonaws.com",
                        [`${url}:sub`]: "system:serviceaccount:default:myapp",
                    },
                },
            }],
        })),
        tags,
    });
    new aws.iam.RolePolicy("app-service-policy", { role: svcRole.id, policy: readAssets });
    serviceIdentityArn = svcRole.arn;
} else {
    const user = new aws.iam.User("app-service-user", { name: `myapp-${stack}-svc`, tags });
    new aws.iam.UserPolicy("app-service-user-policy", { user: user.name, policy: readAssets });
    serviceIdentityArn = user.arn;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTTPS (AC-6) — listener on 443, no forced 80->443 redirect.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const albSg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("alb-sg", {
    vpcId: vpc.id,
    ingress: [{ protocol: "tcp", fromPort: 443, toPort: 443, cidrBlocks: [isProd ? "0.0.0.0/0" : vpc.cidrBlock] }],
    egress: [{ protocol: "-1", fromPort: 0, toPort: 0, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
    tags,
});

const alb = new aws.lb.LoadBalancer("app-alb", {
    internal: !isProd,
    loadBalancerType: "application",
    securityGroups: [albSg.id],
    subnets: subnetIds,
    tags,
});

const tg = new aws.lb.TargetGroup("app-tg", {
    port: 8080, protocol: "HTTP", targetType: "ip", vpcId: vpc.id,
    healthCheck: { path: "/healthz", matcher: "200" },
    tags,
});

const certArn = config.require("certificateArn");

new aws.lb.Listener("app-https", {
    loadBalancerArn: alb.arn,
    port: 443,
    protocol: "HTTPS",
    sslPolicy: "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06",
    certificateArn: certArn,
    defaultActions: [{ type: "forward", targetGroupArn: tg.arn }],
});

let publicEndpoint: pulumi.Output<string> = pulumi.interpolate`https://${alb.dnsName}`;

if (isProd) {
    // CloudFront requires the ACM cert in us-east-1.
    const cdn = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution("app-cdn", {
        enabled: true,
        origins: [{
            originId: "alb",
            domainName: alb.dnsName,
            customOriginConfig: {
                httpPort: 80, httpsPort: 443,
                originProtocolPolicy: "https-only",
                originSslProtocols: ["TLSv1.2"],
            },
        }],
        defaultCacheBehavior: {
            targetOriginId: "alb",
            viewerProtocolPolicy: "redirect-to-https",
            allowedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD", "OPTIONS"],
            cachedMethods: ["GET", "HEAD"],
            forwardedValues: { queryString: true, cookies: { forward: "none" } },
        },
        restrictions: { geoRestriction: { restrictionType: "none" } },
        viewerCertificate: {
            acmCertificateArn: config.require("cloudfrontCertificateArn"),
            sslSupportMethod: "sni-only",
            minimumProtocolVersion: "TLSv1.2_2021",
        },
        tags,
    });
    publicEndpoint = pulumi.interpolate`https://${cdn.domainName}`;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Outputs — all real Outputs. `dbConnectionString` stays secret-marked.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
export const bucketName = bucket.bucket;
export const bucketEndpoint = pulumi.interpolate`https://s3.${region}.amazonaws.com/${bucket.bucket}`;
export const dbEndpoint = db.endpoint;
export const dbConnection = dbConnectionString;
export const kubeconfig = pulumi.secret(cluster.kubeconfig);
export const serviceIdentity = serviceIdentityArn;
export const appUrl = publicEndpoint;
```

---

## Stack configs (AC-7)

`Pulumi.dev.yaml`
```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  myapp:region: us-east-1
  myapp:certificateArn: arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:111122223333:certificate/dev-xxxx
  myapp:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAJ...ciphertext...
```

`Pulumi.prod.yaml`
```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  myapp:region: us-east-1
  myapp:certificateArn: arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:111122223333:certificate/prod-alb-xxxx
  myapp:cloudfrontCertificateArn: arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:111122223333:certificate/prod-cdn-xxxx
  myapp:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAJ...ciphertext...
```

Two stacks → two independent state files → prod changes can't touch dev state.

---

## Delta summary

| Change | Criterion |
|---|---|
| `await arn` → `pulumi.interpolate` | preview crash fixed, DAG edge preserved |
| `pulumi.output("literal")` → `config.requireSecret` | AC-3 |
| Split `Bucket` → `BucketV2` + versioning/SSE/PAB, + prod CRR | AC-1 |
| `deletionProtection: true`, `backupRetention >= 7`, `storageEncrypted`, `publiclyAccessible: false`, `skipFinalSnapshot: false` | AC-2 |
| Scoped-ARN policies; dev user / prod OIDC role | AC-4 |
| `eks.Cluster` managed node group, sizes from `envSpec` | AC-5 |
| 443 listener + ACM cert, CloudFront in prod, no 80 listener | AC-6 |
| `pulumi.getStack()` drives sizing; per-stack YAML | AC-7 |

Add a guardrail so the `await`-on-Output pattern can't regress:

```jsonc
// .eslintrc.json
{ "rules": { "@typescript-eslint/await-thenable": "error" } }
```
